@harjothkhara Thanks — good catch. Addressed in ece303f85f.

The lossless guard now lstat()s both sides, requires regular files through non-symlink parent chains, compares the restorable permission bits, and only then compares bytes. Stat/read failures also fail closed instead of silently treating the worktree copy as safe.

Added POSIX regression coverage for:
- source 0644 / worktree 0755 with identical bytes;
- a worktree copy replaced by a same-content symlink;
- a source baseline replaced by a same-content symlink.

Each case leaves git status --porcelain clean and now expects removeIfLossless() to return false while preserving the worktree state. Exact-head test-types and Real behavior proof are green; the remaining CI matrix is still settling, and I will refresh the PR Evidence section with the final exact-head results.
